\vspace{0.22cm}
{\Large\bfseries\color{ChapterNavy} 全書一句話 \textperiodcentered\ The Whole Book in One Verse}

\vspace{0.30cm}
\fcolorbox{ScriptureGold}{ScriptureBg}{%
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\centering\vspace{0.2cm}
\normalsize\color{CommentaryBrown}
神非人，必不致\textbf{\color{PromiseGold!80!black}說謊}，也非人子，必不致後悔。\\
祂說話豈不照著行呢？祂發言豈不要\textbf{\color{PromiseGold!80!black}成就}呢？\\[0.5em]
\footnotesize\itshape
God is not a man, that He should \textbf{lie},\\
nor a son of man, that He should repent;\\
has He said, and will He not \textbf{do} it?\\[0.4em]
\small\color{ChapterNavy} 民數記 23:19 \textperiodcentered\ Numbers 23:19
\vspace{0.2cm}
\end{minipage}}

\vspace{0.35cm}
{\small\color{TextGray} 三十六章 \textperiodcentered\ 五卷 \textperiodcentered\ 一個不改變的信實神，帶著一群不斷改變的百姓\\
\textit{Thirty-six chapters \textperiodcentered\ five volumes \textperiodcentered\ one unchanging God, one ever-changing people}}

\vspace{0.30cm}
{\small
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.3}
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{2.8cm}p{2.4cm}p{6.9cm}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{段落} & \textbf{章節} & \textbf{在全書的展開} \\
\midrule
在西奈的次序 & 1-10:10章 & 數點百姓、按支派安營、分別利未人——會幕居中的第一代軍隊整裝待發 \\
曠野的抱怨與審判 & 10:11-20章 & 接連的抱怨、可拉黨的叛變、十二探子的惡信——第一代人在不信中倒斃曠野 \\
從何珥山到摩押平原 & 21-25章 & 銅蛇、巴蘭四次逆轉的祝福、巴力毘珥的淫亂——外邦先知也咒詛不了神所祝福的 \\
新一代的預備 & 26-32章 & 第二次數點、交棒約書亞、河東二支派半求業——新一代重新面對信心的功課 \\
應許之地的產業 & 33-36章 & 曠野路程總回顧、迦南境界、逃城與產業條例——一切都指向即將進入的地 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
}

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textcolor{ScriptureGold}{\rule{2.5in}{0.7pt}}
\vspace{0.22cm}

{\bfseries\color{ChapterNavy} 讀經之鑰 \textperiodcentered\ How to Read This Book}

\vspace{0.15cm}
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\small\color{TextGray}
不是來讀一份枯燥的人口普查與行軍手冊，是來看一位信實的神，如何背負著一群
不斷抱怨的百姓，走完從西奈到應許之地的漫長曠野路。\\
若你讀完三十六章卻只記得「以色列人常常抱怨」——請從頭再讀，\\
這次留意：神從未因百姓的不信而收回祂的應許。\\[0.4em]
\textit{\footnotesize
You are not reading a dry census-and-march manual — you are watching a
faithful God carry a chronically complaining people the whole length of the
wilderness road from Sinai to the promised land.\\
If after thirty-six chapters you remember only "the Israelites kept
complaining," read it again — the LORD never withdrew His promise because of
their unbelief.}
\end{minipage}

\vfill
